  "metaDescription": "Indonesian authorities are intensifying investigations into alleged illegal wiretapping of President Prabowo Subianto, including high-level ethics hearings.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "National Police Chief General Suyudi Ario Seto has pledged firm action against those involved in the alleged illegal surveillance of the President.",
    "The police have initiated ethics hearings for high-ranking officials, including Inspector General Ahrie Sonta, as part of the ongoing investigation.",
    "Witness Protection Agency (LPSK) is currently reviewing reports of intimidation against six witnesses connected to the case."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police are conducting a comprehensive investigation into allegations of illegal wiretapping directed at President Prabowo Subianto. Current efforts include formal ethics hearings led by the Propam Division against senior officers suspected of involvement, such as Inspector General Ahrie Sonta. Police leadership has characterized the incident as an act of betrayal, pledging an accountable and transparent inquiry that extends to the administrative level. Concurrently, the Witness Protection Agency is evaluating reports of threats directed at six witnesses involved in the case. The situation has prompted public figures and legislative members to call for a thorough investigation while highlighting the broader implications for national cyber security. Recent developments also include significant structural changes within the police force, involving the reassignment of two high-ranking police commissioners during the active investigation phase. Authorities continue to urge the public to await the final outcomes of the judicial and internal processes.",
